    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §3, Chap 498 of 2017",
    "lawSection": "General Services, Commissioner of",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S6494\n\nSPONSOR: MAYER\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend chapter 498 of the laws of 2017\nauthorizing the New York state thruway authority to convey real property\nto Rye Country Day School, in relation to requiring the Rye Country Day\nSchool to make the athletic field and track available for rental to\npublic recreation groups for a certain amount of time per year\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nTo provide an alternative method of securing public use of a recreation\nparcel being sold by New York State to a not-for-profit school for\nrecreational and educational uses.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection three is amended to read as follows:\n\n§ 3. The authorization to transfer and convey the lands described in\nsection four of this act shall be contingent upon the inclusion of a\ncovenant providing that Rye Country Day School shall make the athletic\nfield and track available for rental to public recreation groups for no\nless than twenty-nine percent of usable hours in the course of each\ncalendar year and to provide opportunity for public rental of any recre-\nation buildings that may be constructed on the parcel.   \nDIFFERENCE\nBETWEEN ORIGINAL AND AMENDED VERSION (IF APPLICABLE):\n\n n/a\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation amends Chapter 498 of the Laws of 2017 which authorized\nthe sale of state land to Rye Country Day School, a not-for-profit\ncorporation chartered by the Board of Regents of the University of the\nState of New York for recreational and educational use by the school and\nthe public.\n\nThat legislation established a process for the school and the city to\nagree to a use plan for school and public use of the parcel. Discussions\ntowards such a use plan have not been completed. To insure that the\ncommunity, through school acquisition, retains the opportunity to secure\nthe parcel for the benefit of school and public recreation groups\ncontemplated in 2017 legislation, this measure provides an alternate\nmethod of assuring public use through the inclusion of a deed covenant\nby the school before transfer from the state can proceed. Utilization of\nthis covenant will only be necessary if the city and school fail to come\nto agreement.\n\nThe twenty-nine percent of field and track time for public use included\nin the legislation matches the amount of time detailed in the proposal\nby the school which was the basis for their willingness to commit to a\nmajor capital program to acquire the parcel and develop the site at\ntheir cost.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nThis is a new bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nn/a\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
